{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/602302-kin-or-not-a-kin-the-fandom-edition","id":602302,"title":"Kin or not a Kin? -the Fandom Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-24T15:30:05-07:00","id":602302,"title":"Kin or not a Kin? -the Fandom Edition","content":"Since Beast's preview was out, the question which hunter may be considered as a &quot;Kin&quot; was asked a number of times. While I hope that the new Mortal Remains chapter would answer that question, I've thought that since I've made a number of hunter conspiracies I could answer that question to my homebrew for those who may use them in a Beast Chronicle. Also, anyone else who have made a group is welcomed to answer which of their groups are Kin in this thread!<br /> <br /> Anyway, here is my list-<br /> <br /> <b>the Pythian Oracles</b>- Kin. Not only that some of them are true Slashers, all of them carry the Serpent's Venom (either from birth or from the potion) and as such are transformed into a something a bit less.. human.<br /> <b>Raziel LtD</b>- not a Kin. While only the members of the company can use TT, this is a part of the Infrastructure and use a lot of G-M tech. Nothing for Beasts to relate to. Even those who can read the Book are connected to the Machine, not the Mother.<br /> <b>Silent Imperative</b>- depends. Is their Endowment a mundane power? If not, is it just a magical trick? Or maybe it is a real transforming process powerd by stolen rites of the Lucifuge?<br /> <b>Cage of Shadows</b>- I don't think so. I mean, mentally they are more than a &quot;Kin&quot;, but their shadow manipulation is the same as the MM's Endowment- a power granted by someone else.<br /> <b>Aki Ten-</b> most of them are not a Kin, just people with occult knowledge and advanced tech- sure, they have a Rank, but it is an honorably one. Those who are Spirit Beloved, however, are Kin, and so are their Shikigami.<br /> <b>E.V.E Institution</b>- Kin. So. Much. Kin.<br /> Museum Secretorum- only as long as they have a witch coated in amber in the storage room.<br /> <b>Ashen Collective</b>- only once they hit Status 5 and start getting access to the Elixir, and only as long as they are under its effect. They Homunculi, however, are.<br /> <b>Orchestra Fatalibus</b>- I'm not sure. Their songs are supernatural (or at least, seem that way) but I they come from a human heart. In fact, being human is what defines the group. Their songs are about people, not monsters.<br /> <b>Ebony Fangs</b>- only young members of Status 1 are not Kin. Once they hit Status 2, their connection with the Underworld turns them into inhuman enough for Beasts to relate to.<br /> <b>Temple of Silence</b>- again, granted blessings and human heart. Not a Kin.<br /> <b>Maagal HaBaal VeHaAshera-</b> Are Sekhem Sorcerers count? If not, they are Kin only in Status 5, where the exposure to Sekhem is enough to really change them. If they do, then they are Kin since the beginning.<br /> <b>Maw of the River</b>- Kin. They supernaturally hidden, eat relics, hit patchwork in the face and drain the Devourer's chosen to death. Those guys are way outside of humanity.<br /> <b>Theater of Tragedies</b>- Not a Kin. Their powers are based around hacking to the G-M. Nothing about the Dark Mother.<br /> <b>Nimrod Movement</b>- Not a Kin. Even if you count their rituals (and you shouldn't) they come from the G-M, not the D-M*<br /> <b>Heirs of the Crown</b>- not in demon state? not a Kin. While having their demons in their body? Depends on what those demons are, and if they are part of the Beast Mythos<br /> <b>Navio de Tolos</b>- most of the members are not a Kin, but Captain are. I mean, they have a moving Lair which they use to travel the Primordial Dream! They are actually mini-Beasts, in a way.<br /> <br /> hope it helps! :P<br /> <br /> *Also, just noticed- bot the Abbreviations of the God Machine AND the Dark Mother are names for the &quot;RPG hosts&quot;- Game Master and Dungeon Master. Now we only need a godly being with ST as an abbreviation and we are good to go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-24-2015, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}